# Android Project Engineering Standards

## Purpose

This directory defines how engineers and AI agents should add or change code in the existing Android project.

These are not generic Android templates. They are standards for this Android codebase, based on the architecture and patterns already present in the project. Do not use them to invent a new structure when the current project already has an established path.

Sensitive values, credentials, signing details, Firebase files, private test config, and exact environment secrets must not be copied into standards docs.

## Current Project Anchors

- Single Gradle module: `:app`.
- App code: `app/src/main/java/com/dailywire/thedailywire`.
- Unit and Robolectric tests: `app/src/test`.
- Instrumentation and E2E tests: `app/src/androidTest`.
- Shared test fixtures: `app/src/testFixtures`.
- Room schema history: `app/schemas`.
- Main build config: `app/build.gradle.kts`.
- Dependency catalog: `gradle/libs.versions.toml`.

```text
.
├── app/
│   ├── build.gradle.kts
│   ├── schemas/
│   └── src/
│       ├── main/
│       │   └── java/com/dailywire/thedailywire/
│       ├── test/
│       ├── androidTest/
│       └── testFixtures/
├── gradle/
│   └── libs.versions.toml
├── AGENTS.md
└── TESTING.md
```

